{"declarations":[{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/StringLitProof.html#Lean.Meta.mkStringLitCodeProof\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">mkStringLitCodeProof</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">s</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#String\">String</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Prod\">×</a> <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Builds a proof of `String.Internal.code s = n` for the string literal `s`, where `n` is the\nnumeral `stringLitCode s`. Returns `n` and the proof.\n\nTo check it, the kernel evaluates `String.Internal.codeOfList` on the list of characters of `s`.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/StringLitProof.html#Lean.Meta.mkStringLitCodeProof","kind":"def","line":45,"name":"Lean.Meta.mkStringLitCodeProof","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Meta/StringLitProof.lean#L45-L54"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/StringLitProof.html#Lean.Meta.stringLitCode\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">stringLitCode</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">s</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#String\">String</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Returns the code of the string `s`: the value of `String.Internal.code s`.\nSee `String.Internal.codeOfList`.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/StringLitProof.html#Lean.Meta.stringLitCode","kind":"def","line":38,"name":"Lean.Meta.stringLitCode","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Meta/StringLitProof.lean#L38-L43"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/StringLitProof.html#Lean.Meta.mkStringLitNeProof\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">mkStringLitNeProof</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">s₁ </span><span class=\"fn\">s₂</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#String\">String</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Basic.html#Lean.Meta.MetaM\">MetaM</a> <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Builds a proof of `String.ofList l₁ ≠ String.ofList l₂` for two distinct string literals.\n\nThe proof is `String.Internal.ofList_ne_ofList l₁ l₂ i (Eq.refl false)` where `i` is the first\nposition where the two strings differ. If one of them is a prefix of the other, `i` is the length\nof the shorter one.\n\nTo check it, the kernel evaluates `String.Internal.sameCharAt i l₁ l₂`, which traverses the first\n`i` elements of the two lists simultaneously without comparing them, and then compares the\ncharacters at position `i`. It does not unfold `String.decEq`.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/StringLitProof.html#Lean.Meta.mkStringLitNeProof","kind":"def","line":16,"name":"Lean.Meta.mkStringLitNeProof","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Meta/StringLitProof.lean#L16-L36"}}],"imports":["Init.Data.String.Csimp","Lean.Meta.AppBuilder"],"instances":[],"name":"Lean.Meta.StringLitProof"}